# Integration notes & rigor flags (added by coordinating session — resolve before deck is final)

This plan is the canonical slide/figure design. These are not edits to it —
they are open items that must be settled so the deck survives a Royal Society Q&A.

**Resolved rigor flag 1 — predator recovery is context, not the promoted HG
cause.** The earlier "predator recovery, not climate" wording is removed. S9
now leads with the robust HG result (spatial/portfolio erosion and uneven
post-closure recovery) and treats predator recovery as a plausible, large, but
not yet promoted pressure. S10 uses Doherty 2025 only as the WCVI mechanism
analogue and pairs it with Surma & Pitcher 2015 plus the current model ledger:
`m5_stier_predation_pressure` and `m5_stier_predator_demand_total` are held
screens with no material calibration gain. If a Q&A asks "is predation the
cause?", the answer is: *not proven for HG; large enough to prioritize data,
not clean enough to promote a coefficient.*

**Citations already corrected/confirmed (consistent with this plan):** S15
cognitive maps = **Stier et al. 2016 *Conservation Letters* 10(1):67–76,
N=27** ✅ acquired. McKechnie 2014, Shelton 2014, Stier 2020 Ecosphere,
Samhouri 2017 ✅ in dossier (image-PDFs). Cleary 2024 = **DFO CSAS Science
Response 2025/005** (S18 source) — source-resolved through the core DFO public
extraction workflow. Gerrard 2014 ✅ acquired (backup-only per plan).

**Theory framing still recommended (v2 §theory spine):** the separability /
management-window thesis pairs naturally with Rocha et al. 2018 *Science*
(coupled/cascading regime shifts; Levin co-author) and Lenton 2008 / Lenton's
positive-tipping keynote — both acquired. Worth one explicit citation in S2/S20
so the thesis reads as connected to the forum's own vocabulary.

**Wire-in data dependencies (must come from the core analysis, not the early
abstract — firewall): RECONCILED.** Current-analysis numbers (synchrony
0.63 all-11 / 0.70 focal-9; Simpson effective sections 3.26 / 3.31; recent-
period top-three share 84%) → cite `Output/diagnostics/m1_stier_11_portfolio_metrics.md`.
The "2.1×" and "65% local vs 4% archipelago" are **Stier et al. 2020 published
results**, NOT `m1_stier_11` outputs — keep them labelled "(Stier et al.
2020)", never as current. Do not use the early abstract's "7 of 9 since 1994"
phrasing as a current number. Full mapping:
`talk-usuk-forum-2026/Talk_Materials/numbers_provenance.md`. S18 LRP /
37.8%-below-LRP / "0 t" → from Cleary 2024 SR 2025/005.

**Cross-refs:** narrative/citation map = `talk_outline_v2.md`; hypotheses &
counter-arguments = `docs/herring-non-recovery-hypotheses.md`; assets =
`docs/HERRING_TALK_ASSETS.md` §3 + the dossier `Reference_Papers/`.

